  THE GENERAL COROLLARY [PROOF — two lines, from two gated
  ingredients; printed, not gated, because it is algebra.
  ROUND-1 BLOCKER 1: it proves an IMPLICATION, and the first
  delivery of this unit read it as an equivalence.  Its actual
  hypothesis is stated first, its sufficiency second]:
    THE HYPOTHESIS THE PROOF USES is exactly one equation:
        Z(Hab) = Z(Hba)   for every commuting pair.
    (depth, sigma)-factoring — Z(h) = Zhat(|h|, sigma(h)) — is
    ONE SUFFICIENT CONDITION for it, and a very special one.
    Given that hypothesis, for every COMMUTING pair,
        P_Z(a|H) P_Z(b|Ha) = q(a|H) q(b|Ha) Z(Hab) / Z(H)
        P_Z(b|H) P_Z(a|Hb) = q(b|H) q(a|Hb) Z(Hba) / Z(H)
    (both telescope), and the two right-hand sides are EQUAL:
    the raw products agree by DC1(b) [gated above, 0
    exceptions], and Z(Hab) = Z(Hba) by hypothesis — which for
    a (depth, sigma)-factoring Z holds because |Hab| = |Hba|
    and sigma(Hab) = sigma(Hba) is the definition of the
    commuting class.  So the DC1 defect is annihilated by ANY
    completion satisfying the displayed equation.
    WHAT THE PROOF DOES NOT GIVE, and the first delivery
    wrongly took from it: (a) it does not say the corpus's
    completions are the ONLY repairs — the solution space of
    the displayed equation is measured in DC1-R below and is
    573-dimensional at the depth-4 truncation, against 28 for
    the (depth, sigma) family; and (b) it says NOTHING about
    DESCENT — 'mu_Z is a function of the record' is a
    different and inequivalent system of equations, and
    DC1-R(e)/(f) exhibit positive completions separating the
    two conditions in BOTH directions.
    THE CORPUS HAS A COMPLETION THAT DOES BOTH.  D49's
    root-free Zhat(h) = 2^(-|h|) . f(class(sigma(h)))
    (lambda = 2, f = (4,4,3,7,3,3)/3) has the factoring shape,
    is normalised per cut at every depth at this scope, and —
    gated below in DC1-R(h), where the first delivery only
    asserted it — its measure mu_Zhat = q.Zhat IS constant on
    every record class of the family.  So Zhat genuinely
    descends.  The price is named and unchanged: D50 — the
    stationary FORM of Z is a CHOICE, i.e. supplied, not
    derived; DC1-R now puts a number on that choice.  That is
    why DC4 item 2 stands as supplied and is priced rather
    than moved.

[DC1-R — THE REPAIR SPACE (round-1 BLOCKER 1).  Setup, and it
 is d42b3's own gradient construction: truncate at depth D; let
 Z be FREE and positive on the depth-D histories and extend it
 downward by the completion recursion Z(h) = sum_e q(e|h)
 Z(h+e), which is exactly what makes P_Z(e|h) = q Z(h+e)/Z(h)
 a normalised kernel.  Then:
   * Z REPAIRS the defect  <=>  Z(Hab) = Z(Hba) for every
     commuting pair whose square closes inside the truncation
     (given DC1(b), this is necessary AND sufficient — see the
     corollary above).  A LINEAR system.
   * Z DESCENDS  <=>  mu_Z = q.Z is a function of the record,
     i.e. Z is constant on record classes (q is, gated in
     DC1-R(i)).  A DIFFERENT linear system.
 Z == 1 solves both, so each solution space meets the positive
 orthant in an OPEN cone and every dimension below is a
 dimension of strictly positive completions.]

  record classes by depth = [1, 6, 23, 84, 313, 1138, 3983], total 5548  (d42b3's committed canon; the same layer census D49 reports)

  D = 4:  free variables (depth-4 histories) = 976;  repair constraints = 403;
            EXACT rational rank = 403  ->  dim of the POSITIVE REPAIR CONE = 573
  [PASS] DC1-R(a) THE REPAIR CONE IS 573-DIMENSIONAL AT THE DEPTH-4 TRUNCATION [SUBSTANTIVE — this is the number the first delivery never computed, and the whole of round-1's BLOCKER].  The necessary-and-sufficient repair condition Z(Hab) = Z(Hba) is a linear system on the free boundary values; its exact rational rank is computed by sparse elimination over Q (no modular shortcut, no float).  Every solution is a completion under which the generated law's completed kernel satisfies EVERY commuting-square identity the census tests  (variables = 976, constraints = 403, exact rank = 403 (the constraints are independent), dim = 573)
  [PASS] DC1-R(b) THE (depth, sigma) FAMILY IS A 28-DIMENSIONAL SLICE OF THE 573-DIMENSIONAL CONE [SUBSTANTIVE]: the completions the dichotomy line forced are the ones constant on the sigma classes of the boundary cut; each of its basis vectors is verified to satisfy ALL of the repair equations (the corollary, instantiated), and it leaves 545 independent directions of strictly positive repairs TRANSVERSE to the corpus's family.  The same line gates the containment that places this family INSIDE the descending one: record identity implies sigma identity on every record class of the family — a property of THIS record functor (residue 3), not a general fact  (dim (depth,sigma) family = 28 (= the sigma states realised at depth 4); repair-equation violations across its 28 basis vectors = 0; transverse directions = 545; record classes carrying two sigma values = 0 of 5548)
  [PASS] DC1-R(c) THE DESCENDING SUB-CONE IS 205-DIMENSIONAL [SUBSTANTIVE]: a completion DESCENDS when mu_Z = q.Z is a function of the record, i.e. (q being record-constant, DC1-R(i)) when Z is constant on record classes.  That family is 313-dimensional at the boundary cut and — gated, not assumed — its constancy PROPAGATES downward through the recursion to every record class of every shallower depth.  Intersecting it with the repair system gives the completions that do BOTH  (dim record-constant family = 313 (= record classes at depth 4); downward-propagation violations = 0 over 427 record classes at depths 0..4; rank of the repair system ON that family = 108; dim of repairs THAT ALSO DESCEND = 205)
  [PASS] DC1-R(d) SQUARE-REPAIR AND DESCENT ARE DIFFERENT CONDITIONS, AND THE HIERARCHY IS STRICT [SUBSTANTIVE — the direct refutation of the first delivery's 'the completions the dichotomy line forced are PRECISELY the objects that repair descent'].  Neither family contains the other: the repair cone (573) is not inside the record-constant family (313) and the record-constant family is not inside the repair cone, since their intersection is a proper subspace of each; and a repair equation is implied by record-constancy exactly when its two corners share a record  (repair cone 573 vs intersection 205 (so repairs are NOT all descents); record-constant 313 vs intersection 205 (so descents are NOT all repairs); repair rows NOT implied by record-constancy = 152 of 403 (= exactly the 152 rows whose two corners carry DIFFERENT records))

  WITNESS (i) — A POSITIVE COMPLETION THAT REPAIRS EVERY
  SQUARE AND DOES NOT DESCEND.  Construction, deterministic:
  the kernel vectors of the repair system are read off the
  exact echelon in free-column order, each scaled to
  max|v| = 1; the FIRST one that is not record-constant is
  taken and Z = 1 + v/100 (so 99/100 <= Z <= 101/100 at the
  boundary and Z > 0 everywhere).  Result: free column 19,
  kernel support 4 — Z > 0: True; repair-equation violations: 0 of 403;
  record classes carrying TWO different mu_Z values: 2 (sizes [4, 6]).
  [The round-1 referee's own witness of this shape reported 4 violated
  record-constancy equations with a size-4 class; the exact counts are
  a property of WHICH kernel direction is taken — the verdict is not.]
  [PASS] DC1-R(e) WITNESS (i): 'ANNIHILATES THE DEFECT' DOES NOT IMPLY 'DESCENDS' [SUBSTANTIVE — it fails if every repair is record-constant, which is what the first delivery's 'precisely' would require].  A strictly positive completion that satisfies EVERY commuting-square identity the census tests, and whose induced measure mu_Z = q.Z is NOT a function of the record: a single record class carries two different masses, so P_Z is not the conditional system of any measure on record cylinders  (positive = True, repair violations = 0/403, record classes with two mu values = 2)

