  *** DC1-R VERDICT — THE HIERARCHY (round-1 BLOCKER 1) ***
    repair cone (573)  STRICTLY CONTAINS
    repairs that also descend (205)  STRICTLY CONTAINS
    the (depth, sigma) family (28)  STRICTLY CONTAINS
    the depth-stationary ray (1) = D49's Zhat
    [at D = 5: 3053 / 32 — the gap widens with depth]
    Reading it in words.  The descent defect names the JOB a
    completion has to do; it does NOT single out the corpus's
    completions among the objects that do it.  What collapses
    the cone to one ray is D50's FORM choice — depth-stationary
    factoring through sigma — which is supplied, not derived,
    and is now a number rather than an adjective.  The two
    lines therefore MEET more weakly than the first delivery
    said: the corpus's completions are AMONG the repairs (and
    Zhat's measure genuinely descends, DC1-R(h)), but 'the
    completions the dichotomy line forced are PRECISELY the
    objects that repair descent' is FALSE IN BOTH DIRECTIONS
    (DC1-R(e), DC1-R(f)).  The successor question sharpens to:
    is there any RECORD-LEVEL demand that cuts the cone down to
    the family, or is the family selected only by the form?
  [t = 292.4s]

