  DC3(2) DECOHERENCE OF THE QUERIED RECORD ALGEBRA [REPORTING ONLY — TRIVIALLY SATISFIED AND THEREFORE
  UNINFORMATIVE; there is NO gate here that could fail, and
  the pin (§2, DC3 clause 2) requires this to be said plainly].
    The generated law is a CLASSICAL stochastic process on
    records: sigma is a serialised finite state, the menu is a
    finite set of exact Fraction weights, and the queried
    algebra is the algebra of history cylinders itself.  A
    classical process has a diagonal decoherence functional by
    construction, so hypothesis (2) holds for the empty reason.
    WHERE THE REMAINING MAP SEGMENT LIVES: paper 29's
    hypothesis (2) is a condition on class OPERATORS and their
    Gram functional D(alpha,beta) = <v_alpha, v_beta> (§4.1,
    §4.2).  The generated line has NO functional level at all —
    no amplitudes, no class operators, no Gram functional, and
    hence no non-trivial decoherence condition to satisfy or
    violate.  This unit does NOT create one.  So the segment of
    the missing map that runs from a decoherence functional to
    the generated record measure is UNTOUCHED here, and it is
    exactly the segment where D59's items 'record instrument'
    and 'preferred durable algebra' still sit.
