[VERDICT]
  SCOPE (non-negotiable): two-actor DELIVERY-FREE d42a, the
  exhaustive depth-6 family.  Nothing below is licensed
  beyond it, and nothing below transfers to the identified
  (action-line) click law: paper 29's map remains open.

  DC1(f) — THE LOAD-BEARING TEST — FAILS.  THE FAILURE IS
  THE DELIVERABLE (pin §2/§4).
  32256 of 425334 REFINED-RECORD-IDENTICAL
  ordered pairs violate P(a|H)P(b|Ha) = P(b|H)P(a|Hb).
  On the wider sigma-commuting class (DC1(a), the pin's
  coarser predicate) the count is 88632 of 665286 —
  but 56376 of those failures lie OUTSIDE
  Theorem 1's hypothesis, which paper 29 §3.1 explicitly
  exempts, and carry no descent content (DC1-R(f) exhibits a
  genuine record measure that fails the same wider test).
  The structure of the failure is COMPLETE:
    - the RAW products always agree (DC1(b), gated), so
      the generated law's unnormalised history weight IS
      order-independent on commuting pairs — and, more
      strongly, q is constant on every record class
      (DC1-R(i)).  It is NOT a measure: the cut masses
      are ['1', '2', '4', '257/32', '1037/64', '2101/64', '68313/1024'], so q is not additive
      along cuts, which is why a completion is needed;
    - the entire defect is the NORMALISATION: exactly
      d = M(sigma(Hb))/M(sigma(Ha)), the coboundary of the
      per-state menu mass (DC1(c), gated) — a MASS-RATIO
      COCYCLE, the pin's pre-registered structural
      fallback, in its sharpest form;
    - the defect spectrum is exactly {'1': 576654, '4/5': 44316, '5/4': 44316};
      and it is a function of (sigma(H), class(a),
      class(b)) alone under both key resolutions (DC1(d),
      gated) — 616 classes, which with DC1(i)'s
      720 class-level facts is the census's real
      information content;
    - it VANISHES exactly on same-mass intermediates and
      occurs at every mass-mixed pair (DC1(e), gated) —
      the pin's lean was right, and nothing else fails.
  CONSEQUENCE, stated exactly and no wider: there is NO
  positive measure on refined record cylinders at this
  scope whose conditionals are the generated NORMALISED
  kernel — paper 29 Theorem 1's contrapositive, applied to
  a system that satisfies its three positivity hypotheses
  (DC3(4), gated) and its cylinder-identity hypothesis
  (DC1(f), the refined sub-census, gated).
  This does NOT contradict Theorem 1 (a theorem), and it is
  NOT an F1 hit: F1 asks for a MEASURE with unequal
  products; what is exhibited is a conditional system that
  is not induced by any such measure.  The generated law is
  ORDER-WEIGHTED at the normalised level, and any map from
  the action line's conditional-measure reading to it must
  carry order data or supply a completion.
  AND THE DEFECT IS REPAIRABLE, BUT NOT ONLY BY THE CORPUS'S
  COMPLETIONS (DC1-R): the repair cone has dimension
  573 at the depth-4 truncation, of which 205
  dimensions also descend and 28 are the (depth, sigma)
  family; the corpus's Zhat is one ray inside it whose
  measure genuinely descends (DC1-R(h)).  Square-repair and
  descent imply each other in NEITHER direction (DC1-R(e),
  DC1-R(f)).  The descent defect names the JOB the corpus's
  completions do; it does not single them out.

  DC2 — RESTATEMENT, satisfied.  pi = sigma; fibre constancy
  is (H1); the 36-row kernel is printed.  NOT A NEW RESULT.
  DC3 — (1) SUBSTANTIVE, PASS; (2) reporting-only, trivially
  satisfied and uninformative; (3) = DC1(a), FAIL; (4) SUBSTANTIVE,
  PASS; (5) = DC2, restatement.
  DC4 — NO item moves; all six stand (round-1 MAJOR 2).  The
  generated line's own derived boundary statistic is stated
  beside the ledger, not on it.

  THE FAIL COUNT, READ HONESTLY (round-1 MAJOR 3): the FAILs
  below are TWO statements, not one and not three — DC1(a)
  (= DC3(3), literally the same predicate) and DC1(f), which is
  a different predicate over a different population under a
  strictly stronger hypothesis, and is the only one of them
  paper 29's theorem speaks to.

